T \propto r^{3/2}
$$
\frac{T_{2}}{T_{1}} = \left(\frac{r_{2}}{r_{1}}\right)^{3/2}
$$
$$
\frac{\omega_{2}}{\omega_{1}} = \left(\frac{r_{1}}{r_{2}}\right)^{3/2} = (1.21)^{3/2}
$$
$$
\omega_{2} = \omega_{1} (1.331) \quad \text{... (i)}
$$
$$
(\omega_{2} + \omega_{1}) t_{0} = 2\pi \quad \text{... (ii)}
$$
$$
t_{0} = \frac{2\pi}{\omega_{2} + \omega_{1}} = \frac{2\pi}{\left(\frac{4}{3} + 1\right) \omega_{1}} = \frac{6\pi}{7\omega_{1}}
$$
$$
t_{0} = \frac{6\pi (T_{\text{GSS}})}{2\pi (7)}
$$
$$
t_{0} = \frac{3 \times 24 \text{ hours}}{7} = \frac{24}{p} \text{ hours}
$$
$$
p = \frac{7}{3} = 2.33
$$
The value of p is 2.33.
